---
import Legal from '../layouts/Legal.astro';
import { contact, site } from '../data/site';
---

<Legal
  title="Terms of use"
  description="The rules for using TOEFLY: accounts, plans and payments, acceptable use, tutor materials and AI estimates."
  updated="2026-11-23"
  version="0.1"
>
  <h2>The service</h2>
  <p>
    TOEFLY helps you prepare for the TOEFL iBT with weekly study plans, practice tasks, AI feedback and mock exams, and
    gives tutors tools to guide their students. By creating an account you accept these terms and the
    <a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a>. You must be 16 or older.
  </p>

  <h2>Your account</h2>
  <p>
    Keep your sign-in details to yourself and tell us if you think someone else has used your account. You can delete
    your account at any time in Settings.
  </p>

  <h2>Plans and payments</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>The Free plan includes the diagnostic, one week and 10 AI checks of Writing and Speaking.</li>
    <li>Pro, Tutor and Tutor Plus are monthly subscriptions. New learners get 7 days of Pro for free.</li>
    <li>
      Prices are shown on the <a href="/#pricing">pricing section</a> and include VAT for customers in the EU.
    </li>
    <li>
      You can cancel a subscription in Settings, Billing. While TOEFLY is in development, payments run in test mode.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Do not use TOEFLY to cheat on a real exam or to help anyone else do so.</li>
    <li>Do not try to break, overload or get around the limits of the service.</li>
    <li>Do not upload material you have no right to share.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Tutors and their materials</h2>
  <p>
    Tutors are responsible for the books and files they upload and for having the right to use them with their students.
    We remove material when a rights holder asks us to.
  </p>

  <h2>Study material</h2>
  <p>
    Some tasks are based on published preparation materials, and each task names its source. Rights holders can ask for
    removal through <a href={contact.href}>{contact.label}</a>; see{' '}
    <a href="/#sources">where the study material comes from</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>AI estimates</h2>
  <p>
    Predicted bands, AI scores and AI feedback are estimates to guide your study. They are not official scores and do
    not guarantee any result on the TOEFL iBT.
  </p>

  <h2>Trademarks</h2>
  <p>{site.trademark}</p>

  <h2>Liability</h2>
  <p>
    We work to keep TOEFLY available and accurate, but provide it as is. To the extent the law allows, we are not liable
    for exam results or for losses from using the service.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>When these terms change, we tell you in the app and ask you to accept the new version.</p>
</Legal>
